{
  "uid": "rio-chunk-cache-tier",
  "title": "rio-build: Chunk Cache Tier",
  "tags": ["rio-build", "store", "chunk-cache"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {"from": "now-1h", "to": "now"},
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Express tier reads: hit / miss / error",
      "description": "rio_store_tiered_local_{hits,misses,errors}_total rates — TieredChunkBackend get() path. hit = chunk served from the per-AZ S3 Express bucket (no S3-standard RTT); miss = fell through to S3 standard (then write-through filled Express); error = Express read failed (degraded, falls through). All zero/empty when store.chunkBackend.kind != tiered or the replica's AZ has no Express bucket.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_local_hits_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "local hit",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_local_misses_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "miss (S3-standard fallback)",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_local_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "read error (degraded)",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Express tier hit ratio",
      "description": "tiered_local_hits / (hits + misses) — the spec's tiered_local_hit_ratio, computed in PromQL from the counters the backend emits. Expect this to climb toward ~1.0 on warm chunk sets after the cache tier is enabled; gaps mean no tiered get() traffic in the window.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_local_hits_total[5m])) / (sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_local_hits_total[5m])) + sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_local_misses_total[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "hit ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "color": {"mode": "thresholds"},
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "red", "value": null},
              {"color": "yellow", "value": 0.5},
              {"color": "green", "value": 0.8}
            ]
          },
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 20, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "single", "sort": "none"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Express write-through failures",
      "description": "rate(rio_store_tiered_writethrough_errors_total[5m]) — the chunk was served from S3 standard but the Express fill failed, so the next read of the same chunk pays the S3-standard RTT again. Sustained nonzero means Express PUTs are failing (throttling, IAM, bucket missing for this AZ).",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 8, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_tiered_writethrough_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "write-through errors/s",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "thresholds"},
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "yellow", "value": 0.01},
              {"color": "red", "value": 0.1}
            ]
          },
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 20, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "single", "sort": "none"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "In-process chunk cache (moka): hits vs misses",
      "description": "rio_store_chunk_cache_{hits,misses}_total rates — the per-replica in-memory verified-chunk LRU in front of whichever ChunkBackend is configured. Sits above the Express tier: a moka hit never reaches the tiered backend at all.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 8, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_chunk_cache_hits_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "hits/s",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_chunk_cache_misses_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "misses/s",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Chunk dedup ratio per upload",
      "description": "rio_store_chunk_dedup_ratio — per-upload dedup (1.0 - missing/total after chunking), set by the most recent PutPath/PutPathChunked on each replica. Near 1.0 = mostly duplicate content (warm store); near 0.0 = novel content.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 16, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rio_store_chunk_dedup_ratio",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Builder upload chunks: novel vs deduped",
      "description": "rate(rio_builder_upload_chunks_total[5m]) by kind — PutPathChunked outcome as seen from the builder. kind=novel: absent per HasChunks, body sent as a Chunk frame; kind=deduped: already durable, only the manifest entry sent. deduped/(novel+deduped) is the builder-observed durable-presence ratio.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 16, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (kind) (rate(rio_builder_upload_chunks_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{kind}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "PutPathChunked verification failures",
      "description": "increase[5m] of the PutPathChunked verify-walk failure counters. incomplete = stream ended before all novel chunks arrived; verify unavailable = chunk store unreachable during verify; nar_hash / refs / file_digest mismatch = the assembled output does not match what the builder claimed (file_digest mismatch is a castore identity violation — paged by RioStoreFileDigestMismatch).",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 24, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_store_putpath_incomplete_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "incomplete stream",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_store_putpath_verify_unavailable_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "verify unavailable",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_store_narhash_mismatch_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "nar_hash mismatch",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_store_refs_mismatch_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "refs mismatch",
          "refId": "D"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_store_file_digest_mismatch_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "file_digest mismatch",
          "refId": "E"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {"mode": "thresholds"},
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "red", "value": 1}
            ]
          },
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 20, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Store authn rejects by reason",
      "description": "rate(rio_store_hmac_rejected_total[5m]) by reason — requests rejected by the store's HMAC token checks (missing/invalid assignment tokens, service callers not allowlisted or not permitted, builder-role tokens on legacy PutPath). A step change after a deploy usually means key or role-claim drift, not an attack.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 24, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(rio_store_hmac_rejected_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "NAR index eager outcomes",
      "description": "rate(rio_store_nar_index_eager_total[5m]) by outcome — eager nar_index/file_digest compute at PutPath. spawned - error = paths indexed without touching the work queue; sustained skipped means nar_index_concurrency is undersized for the upload rate (the indexer_loop picks the slack up later); error = compute failed (indexer_loop retries from storage).",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 32, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(rio_store_nar_index_eager_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "NAR index compute latency p50/p99",
      "description": "rio_store_nar_index_compute_seconds — per-path NAR reassemble + nar_ls + blake3 + persist (eager PutPath path and indexer_loop). The eager path holds the upload's accumulation buffer for this long; a rising p99 with rising eager skipped means the semaphore is the bottleneck.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 32, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(rio_store_nar_index_compute_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rio_store_nar_index_compute_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "none"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Castore directory RPC latency p99",
      "description": "rio_store_directory_get_seconds (GetDirectory recursive BFS over the Directory DAG — the builder mount-time prefetch source) and rio_store_directory_read_seconds (ReadBlob chunk fetch + slice + stream — the castore-FUSE open() fill source), p99. These are the store-side halves of the builder's dag-prefetch and open() latency panels.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 40, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rio_store_directory_get_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "GetDirectory p99",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(rio_store_directory_read_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "ReadBlob p99",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "none"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Has* batch sizes p99 by rpc",
      "description": "histogram_quantile(0.99, rio_store_directory_has_batch_size) by rpc — digest-list length per HasDirectories/HasBlobs/HasChunks call. These RPCs are batch-by-design (the I-110 lesson); a p99 stuck at 1 means some client is calling them per-digest and will hit the PG wall at scale.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 40, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, rpc) (rate(rio_store_directory_has_batch_size_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{rpc}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Castore scope establishment & churn",
      "description": "rate(rio_store_castore_scope_established_total[5m]) — closure scopes established via PresentClosure (verified against the token's signed input_closure_digest, P0591). rio_store_castore_scope_absent_total by resolution — assignment-token reads that arrived without a scope on this replica: derived = rebuilt from pins+references (normal for a fresh replica), denied = answered CASTORE_SCOPE_REQUIRED so the builder re-presents, served = log/rollback mode only. increase(rio_store_castore_scope_mismatch_total[15m]) — presented closure ≠ signed digest (a builder presenting something it was not dispatched with). Sustained absent→denied alongside a quiet established rate means builders are not presenting — cross-check the presenter panel on the castore-fuse dashboard.",
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 48, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(rio_store_castore_scope_established_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "scopes established/s",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (resolution) (rate(rio_store_castore_scope_absent_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "scope absent → {{resolution}}",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(rio_store_castore_scope_mismatch_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "presented ≠ signed digest (15m)",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 10, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Castore scope denials by reason",
      "description": "increase(rio_store_castore_scope_denied_total[15m]) by reason — castore reads denied by closure scoping under enforce mode: out_of_scope (digest only reachable outside the attested closure; the wire answer is an uninformative NOT_FOUND) or unattested (token carries no closure digest; PERMISSION_DENIED). increase(rio_store_castore_scope_would_deny_total[15m]) by reason — what enforce WOULD have denied while running the log rollback mode; it must drain to zero before flipping back to enforce. Any sustained movement here is either a token being replayed outside its build or a presentation/coverage bug — the structured deny log on rio-store carries the drv/executor/digest detail (RioStoreCastoreScopeDenied alert).",
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 48, "w": 12, "h": 8},
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}"},
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (increase(rio_store_castore_scope_denied_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "denied: {{reason}} (15m)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (increase(rio_store_castore_scope_would_deny_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "would-deny (log mode): {{reason}} (15m)",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {"mode": "thresholds"},
          "thresholds": {"mode": "absolute", "steps": [{"color": "green", "value": null}, {"color": "red", "value": 1}]},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "line", "lineInterpolation": "linear", "fillOpacity": 20, "spanNulls": false}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true},
        "tooltip": {"mode": "multi", "sort": "desc"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
